{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1496479-birthrights-and-levelling","id":1496479,"title":"Birthrights and levelling?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-08T03:43:22-08:00","id":1496479,"title":"Birthrights and levelling?","content":"Hi all.<br /> <br /> This question is about birthrights and whether they can be levelled up?<br /> My players are all having visitations around now and are hitting Hero and I feel like the birthrights they had in Origin will now be woefully underpowered so I'm in the process of rewriting them.<br /> <br /> The way i have run the game is that the player purchases a birthright and can add dots based on the xp (5 xp for a new birthright or add a dot to an existing) but the birthrights section offers nothing in how to level up a birthright. <br /> <br /> The exceptions being sacrificing dice pool for flairs/knacks for creatures and Guides levelling as you level but not past their dot rating.<br /> <br /> This is really confusing. <br /> <br /> How Have you out there worked this out?<br /> <br /> Note - the current birthrights in play<br /> A 1dot raven who evolved into a 4dot corviknight<br /> A 2dot cat who can transform into larger felines (currently a leopard) but is now 4dots (serpopard?)<br /> The Cane of St Lazarus <br /> A sickle made by Sif for a creation of Thor.<br /> A bracelet that becomes a shield.<br /> A goat that may or may not be celestial","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27625-lordtom","name":"LordTom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T04:13:25-08:00","id":1496481,"title":"","content":"Mysteries of the World (<a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/315311/Mysteries-of-the-World-The-Scion-Second-Edition-Companion?src=hottest_filtered\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...ttest_filtered</a>) have better rules for that, specially Relics.<br /> <br /> My suggestion for the under balanced is allow them to redo all their birthrights to a Hero level. The transformation from Origin to Hero is not a gain of level, it\u2019s a big change as the Hero is now almost an completely new character. In our table we rebuilt all our characters as heroes with the extra experience we gained during Origin sessions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}